(4) conduct media facilitation; (5) conduct public communication through written, spoken, and visual means; (6) counter misinformation and disinformation; (7) conduct communications and visual effects assessments; and (8) conduct Visual Information operations, to include imagery collection, production, management, archival documentation, and integration with command information, training, operational planning, and decision-support processes. CMF 46 Soldiers must maintain technical proficiency in emerging visual technologies, digital asset management, enterprise information systems, metadata standards, and data-driven communication tools to support Army modernization and future force requirements. They will vigorously pursue progressive military and civilian education in communication strategy, visual information management, instructional media design, records management, and leadership to enhance their professional development and increase the capabilities they provide to commanders and staffs. 1–3. Recommended Career Management Self-Development The proponent recommends the following for self-development and demonstrated excellence:', '22cd38fb5c43d6d76ab2475aacc86f8c8dccab5629641f1417efa1a61c8e723a', 2, 2, '2', 7, null, null, false, null),
